{"ref":"card:question","text":"Can running 2 or 4 independent CPU docking jobs together cut four-case workflow cost while preserving every retained pose?","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:hypothesis","text":"Independent jobs may fill idle host capacity, making unchanged four-case CPU docking at least 1.05 times faster with identical outputs.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:if_lever","text":"At width 2 or 4, both paired four-case workflow speedups reach 1.05 with exact docking and pose equality.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:if_not","text":"Neither width achieves 1.05 in both paired four-case workflow speedups, or output equality fails.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:test_summary","text":"Build separate CPU job commands and output checker; compare original four-case serial workflow, separate serial jobs, and 2/4 concurrent jobs in mirrored order. Require identical outputs and both measured speedups at least 1.05. Reserve 2 instance-hours, USD6.58, with USD10 hard cap.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:closest_prior","text":"Published MEGADOCK docking benchmarks reached 98% scaling at 420 nodes; they measured distributed work, not four jobs competing on one host [prior].","sources":[{"id":"prior","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221127/","quote":"Notably, a high scalability (98%) was obtained with the largest number of nodes (420 nodes)."}]}
{"ref":"card:left_open","text":"Whether 2 or 4 fixed-thread CPU jobs sharing 26 logical CPUs preserve every output and beat serial workflow time by 1.05.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:anchor","text":"Match frozen serial docking outputs and all 50 poses per case, then require identical outputs from each scheduling arm.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"card:limits","text":"No dense-search quality, GPU scheduling, biological efficacy or beyond-four-case inference; two repeats provide an operational screen, not statistical confidence.","sources":[]}
{"ref":"src:prior","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4221127/","quote":"Notably, a high scalability (98%) was obtained with the largest number of nodes (420 nodes).","supports":"Published distributed docking scaling result; unlike same-host fixed-thread concurrency. Search returned this open-access article."}

